# Africa of Hope — Vercel deployment environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The app deploys to Vercel only: the Vite SPA AND the Express API
# (which runs as a serverless function under /api/*) live on the same
# Vercel domain. Set these in:
#   Vercel Dashboard → Project → Settings → Environment Variables

# ── Frontend (browser) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Leave VITE_API_URL EMPTY (or unset) for the Vercel deploy so the app
# calls the API on its own domain (/api/school/...). Only set this if you
# ever point the frontend at a separately-hosted API.
# VITE_API_URL=

# ── Server-side only (the /api serverless function) ──────────
# These power the Express API. They MUST NOT have a VITE_ prefix and are
# never shipped to the browser.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key
# Strong random string used to sign session JWTs. REQUIRED in production —
# the API refuses to start without it.
SESSION_SECRET=your-long-random-secret

# Do NOT set ALLOWED_ORIGINS on Vercel: the frontend and API share an
# origin, so no CORS allow-list is needed. Setting a wrong value will make
# same-origin requests fail.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=
